after 42 years full of questions a  family now has closure metro police  announcing they have solved the cold  case homicide involving kim bryant from  1979. joe mohler joins us live outside  of metro police headquarters with how it  was solved joe  metro says the new dna testing method  helped them figure this out they say  johnny blake preston is responsible for  the murder of kim bryant who was killed  when she was just 16 years old  since 1979 many have wondered who killed  kim bryant the lvmpd homicide section  investigated this case for years the  western high school student was  kidnapped raped and murdered her body  was found in the desert the case went  cold as nobody was ever connected to the  crime until now based on sperm recovered  from the body of kim bryant at autopsy  revealed that johnny blake peterson was  the person who kidnapped sexually  assaulted and murdered kim bryant  peterson was 19 at the time and briefly  went to western as well this was solved  after a donation from philanthropist  justin wu condolences to kim's family we  hope that we provided a little bit of  closure for you the donation helped pay  for a newer dna testing method the lab  was author inc out of texas otherum is  able to provide leads that lead to the  salt dr kristen middleman says they take  a deeper look at dna samples they then  look into a genealogical database used  for law enforcement to link the samples  to family members or family trees that  lead is given to investigators in this  case peterson's family we can take those  cases that have failed all those other  methods and we can still solve them  there's still hope for these families  nobody should have to wait 42 years to  find out who murdered their child  now back out here live it is not known  if brian and peterson knew each other at  the time of the murder there will be no  trial because peterson did die back in  1993 now this is the second case that  has been solved like this here in las  vegas middlemen does say that more cases  will be solved here in the very near  future reporting live outside of metro  headquarters this evening joe mohler  live local now
 

